{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525810-questions-for-vtm-scholars","id":1525810,"title":"Questions for VTM Scholars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-22T14:18:20-08:00","id":1525810,"title":"Questions for VTM Scholars","content":"Hello Guys,<br /> I am searching myself since a long time the answer ti a very specific questions: what Is the &quot;<b>Rising Darkness</b>&quot; forsaw by the Wu-Zao (Watcher Salubri) names in <b>Winds from the East?</b><br /> <br /> This so called Rising Darkness Is mentioned about the Fate of the Wu-Zao bloodline described in Winds from the East; apparently Wu-zaos start to walk along the <b>Golden Order</b> (and Anda) due of this Rising Darkness. Sounds like something important.<br /> <br /> I Hope some of you may have the Answer, It would be really appreciated<br /> <br /> Thank you in Advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26189-wuzaolover","name":"WuZaolover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26189_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T14:57:34-08:00","id":1525811,"title":"","content":"IIRC it was either the large scale destruction of the rest of the Salubri clan or the turning of the Age that led to the Asian undead evolving from what you see in WoD: Blood &amp; Silk into their Kindred of the East forms. Possibly both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T15:50:35-08:00","id":1525813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525810-questions-for-vtm-scholars?p=1525811#post1525811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC it was either the large scale destruction of the rest of the Salubri clan or the turning of the Age that led to the Asian undead evolving from what you see in WoD: Blood &amp; Silk into their Kindred of the East forms. Possibly both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you mind to elaborate these concepts? I am curious cause I do not get immediately the relation to &quot;the Rising Darkness&quot;<br /> <br /> -Why the Destruction of the rest of the Clan would be related to the Golden Horde (which Is hiding the Rising Darkness)? Wu Zao never took a side about the Salubri Demise, and they had the chance to choose, cause they were more interested to Zao-lat decree to Preserve Cainite and make the kindred, as a while, to survive the Turn of the wheel; It Is also stated that some of Wu Zao think that Salubri Destruction Is part of Zao Lat scheme so they do not interfere of have interest. So why they are alarmed by the Rising Darkness if Rising Darkness Is related to Western Salubri Destruction?<br /> <br /> - Also note/Remember that by the time Wu-Zaos while investigating the Rising Darkness of Golden Horde, which led them to West, were actually helping the Wan Kuei (ancestral enemies!) to Hunt Down the Anda and eventually causes their extinction<br /> <br /> - \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bAlso Remember that somehow Kupala, in TC, has interest to have the Mongols/Anda to Invade Transilvania and I Always suspected that this Rising Darkness could have had a connection with Kupala, otherwise would really be a funny coincidence<br /> <br /> Sorry for the textwall, Just trieing to gather as much info as I remember","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26189-wuzaolover","name":"WuZaolover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26189_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T16:41:04-08:00","id":1525814,"title":"","content":"You know how the B&amp;S Hungry Dead had Godbody Disciplines of normal Daoist agents, but the modern ones have spooky goffic versions of them and more starting Po dots as well? That's the rising darkness. It's the growing distance of the Hungry Dead from the 10,000 Immortals over time, as they begin to resemble ambulatory corpses more than immortals, and then demons as the Scorpion Eaters continue to push things further with the completely corrupt Shintai Disciplines. I'm pretty sure it's &quot;just&quot; a consequence of the turning of the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T03:15:59-08:00","id":1525828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WuZaolover</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525810-questions-for-vtm-scholars#post1525810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello Guys,<br /> I am searching myself since a long time the answer ti a very specific questions: what Is the &quot;<b>Rising Darkness</b>&quot; forsaw by the Wu-Zao (Watcher Salubri) names in <b>Winds from the East?</b><br /> <br /> This so called Rising Darkness Is mentioned about the Fate of the Wu-Zao bloodline described in Winds from the East; apparently Wu-zaos start to walk along the <b>Golden Order</b> (and Anda) due of this Rising Darkness. Sounds like something important.<br /> <br /> I Hope some of you may have the Answer, It would be really appreciated<br /> <br /> Thank you in Advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I recall, the gameline never explicitly went into details. But between various books you could kind of put the pieces together. One of the Yama Kings, one in charge of Mongolia (whose name I can't remember off hand), ended up getting a vast amount of power due the Mongol conquests and the amount of people they slaughtered. The Wan Kuei in northern China and Mongolia in the area had set up their own Court, the Black Tortoise Court. As the Yama King's power increased, he ended up corrupting the Black Tortoise Court, turning nearly all of them into Akuma. Eventually the other courts moved against them, put them down and, (if I believe) ended up destroying the Yama King but a massive number of enlightened Wan Kuei were lost in the process.<br /> <br /> This was the Rising Darkness that the Wu-Zao foresaw. Many of the Wan Kuei ended up pointing at the Anda (and the Kindred as a whole) for what happened, painting them servants (ignorant or otherwise) of the Yama Kings and blaming them for the fall of the Black Tortoise Court. It was easier to do that than admit that a Wan Kuei court had falling due to its own flaws. The Anda had no idea what was going on, but ended up being hunted down and wiped outt and this idea of the Kindred being ignorant servants of the Yama King ended up coloring the relationship between the Kindred and Wan Kuei into the modern era.<br /> <br /> *Edit* To add to that, the corruption and destruction of the Black Tortoise Court is often pointed to by Wan Kuei scholars as the moment that the Wheel of Ages turned from the Fourth Age to the Fifth Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-23-2023, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T04:58:25-08:00","id":1525832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525810-questions-for-vtm-scholars?p=1525828#post1525828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was the Rising Darkness that the Wu-Zao foresaw. Many of the Wan Kuei ended up pointing at the Anda (and the Kindred as a whole) for what happened, painting them servants (ignorant or otherwise) of the Yama Kings and blaming them for the fall of the Black Tortoise Court. It was easier to do that than admit that a Wan Kuei court had falling due to its own flaws. The Anda had no idea what was going on, but ended up being hunted down and wiped outt and this idea of the Kindred being ignorant servants of the Yama King ended up coloring the relationship between the Kindred and Wan Kuei into the modern era.</div> </div> </div> </div>His name was Dokhor-Khan, ruler of the Hell of Spiked Chains, inhabited by the souls of mortals that had died in the steppes<br /> After the creation of the Quincunx, around the end of the 12 century, the Kuei-jin attacked the holdings of Dokhor-Khan in the former territories of the Black Tortoise Court, severing him from his input of Tainted Chi, which allowed his rivals, among them Rangda and Tou Mu, to destroy him and add parts of the former Hell to their own territories<br /> We have a bit detailed talk about it in the Wraith Dark Ages History topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I do think also, the Rising Darkness was the dawn of the Fifth Age, the turning of the Wheel <br /> And/or either Dokhor-Khan or the Court-alliance against his forces/influence<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T05:14:21-08:00","id":1525833,"title":"","content":"Thanks. It's been awhile since I last read through all the KotE material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}